            <ArticleTitle>Cholecystokinin-octapeptide antagonizes morphine analgesia in periaqueductal gray of the rat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The analgesic effect of systemic morphine (5 mg/kg, s.c.) was dose-dependently antagonized by CCK-8 administered to the periaqueductal gray (PAG) of the rat. This effect could be reversed by proglumide, a CCK-receptor antagonist. The effect of morphine analgesia was potentiated by proglumide administered to PAG. These results are compatible with the notion that PAG is a strategic site where CCK-8 exerts an antiopioid activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
